    {
      "title": "Webhooks and Delivery Retries",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Webhooks and Delivery Retries",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What a webhook promises",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Webhook== = provider sends an HTTP `POST` to your URL on an event",
                "**Push**, not polling",
                "Consumer must return ==2xx fast==",
                "Delivery is ==at-least-once==, never exactly-once",
                "{red:Duplicates} and {red:out-of-order} events are normal"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Retry policy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Non-2xx or timeout",
                    "sub": "delivery failed",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Backoff + jitter",
                    "sub": "1m, 5m, 30m, 2h",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Retry",
                    "sub": "until max attempts",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Give up",
                    "sub": "dead-letter or disable",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Ack, then process",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Verify",
                    "note": "signature",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Enqueue",
                    "note": "store payload",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Return 200",
                    "note": "immediately",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Worker",
                    "note": "heavy work later",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Provider timeouts are often ==5-10s==",
                "Slow inline work means a timeout, then a needless retry"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Pick the status code",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Return"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Valid, queued",
                  "`200`"
                ],
                [
                  "Valid but ignored (unknown type)",
                  "{green:2xx}"
                ],
                [
                  "Truly invalid request",
                  "{orange:4xx}, many providers still retry"
                ],
                [
                  "Temporary failure (DB down)",
                  "{red:5xx}, retried"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake: 500 on a bad payload",
              "text": "A `500` for a **permanently** bad payload wastes every retry until the provider gives up, and can get the endpoint ==disabled==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "HMAC Signatures and Timestamps",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HMAC Signatures and Timestamps",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Gets Signed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==HMAC-SHA256(secret, signed_payload)== travels in a header",
                "Consumer recomputes and compares: proves **authenticity** and **integrity**",
                "Signed payload = `timestamp + '.' + rawBody`",
                "Timestamp inside the signature binds it to a ==point in time=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Raw body",
                    "sub": "exact bytes",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "t.rawBody",
                    "sub": "signed payload",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "HMAC-SHA256",
                    "sub": "shared secret",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Compare",
                    "sub": "constant time",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Verifying Safely",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Verify the ==raw bytes==, not re-serialized JSON",
                "Reject if |now - t| > ==5 min== (blocks replay)",
                "Compare with `hmac.compare_digest` / `crypto.timingSafeEqual`, never `==`",
                "Rotation: accept ==multiple signatures== in the header"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "import hmac, hashlib, time",
                "def ok(secret, t, raw, sigs):",
                "    if abs(time.time() - int(t)) > 300:",
                "        return False",
                "    msg = t.encode() + b'.' + raw",
                "    mac = hmac.new(secret, msg, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()",
                "    return any(hmac.compare_digest(mac, s) for s in sigs)"
              ],
              "note": "tolerance check, recompute, constant-time compare"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Parser first = broken signature",
              "text": "Reparsing changes whitespace and key order. Keep the **raw body** and verify before parsing."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Idempotent Consumers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Idempotent Consumers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Idempotent Means",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Idempotent== = N deliveries have the **same effect** as one",
                "Needed because delivery is ==at-least-once==",
                "Dedupe on the provider's **event ID** (`evt_123`)",
                "{red:Not} payload hash, {red:not} arrival time"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dedupe in the Database",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Receive",
                    "sub": "evt_123",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "INSERT id",
                    "sub": "UNIQUE column",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Side effect",
                    "sub": "same transaction",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Duplicate key",
                    "sub": "skip, return 200",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "sql",
              "lines": [
                "BEGIN;",
                "INSERT INTO processed_events (event_id)",
                "  VALUES ('evt_123');",
                "UPDATE orders SET status = 'paid' WHERE id = 42;",
                "COMMIT;"
              ],
              "note": "duplicate-key error: ROLLBACK, return 200"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Races and Ordering",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Approach",
                "Concurrent retries"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "SELECT then INSERT",
                  "{red:Races}: both pass the check"
                ],
                [
                  "UNIQUE constraint",
                  "{green:Safe}: one insert wins"
                ],
                [
                  "Redis `SET NX` + TTL",
                  "{green:Safe}: atomic claim"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Out-of-order events are normal",
                "Compare ==version== or timestamp; drop stale events",
                "Or **re-fetch** current state from the provider API"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Let the ==unique constraint== decide, never a prior SELECT. Duplicate means **skip and return 200**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
